        ],
        "explanation": "The ClientPermissionEvaluator change adds Javadoc only. ClientPermissionsV2 denies access when the admin is from another realm or the resource server is missing. Otherwise it grants access only if the evaluated permissions include the exact requested scope. The registerListener change only runs the cleanup when ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ is enabled. V1 and V2 are different versions of the same feature (version 1 and version 2 in Profile.java), so they should not be enabled together. That means the V2 setPermissionsEnabled methods, which throw UnsupportedOperationException, should not be reached from this listener. I did not confirm that mutual exclusion in the profile resolution code.",
